# Day 29

**33km / 8 hours**

Not a difficult day but certainly a long one. It began with a pleasant coastal walk past the water treatment area which is amusing since it's called the Watercare coastal walk as if they're the ones sponsoring it. Also it didn't smell terrible and there were some nice water birds around including many adorable ducklings. 

![Many ducks and ducklings in the water enjoying themselves (I hope)](./ducklings.jpg)

After that there were some archeological areas and whatnot. Some interesting things but I had a proper day ahead so there wasn't time to linger and afterwards there was a lot of road. An interesting part of the road was it going past the airport so I could just watch planes coming in. 

![Certainly not as interesting as a cool bird](./plane.jpg)

There were quite a few construction sites and stream walks and even a section in the botanic gardens but honestly it wasn't that interesting, just a lot of pavement. Onwards and upwards!